  "info": {
    "title": "(s, S) inventory with backorders",
    "category": "Supply chain",
    "description": "(s, S) inventory control with a replenishment lead time and backorders. Stock is a LEVEL; customers are entities that draw from it through a TRANSFER block and WAIT when it is short -- the backorder. A falling threshold at s fires the reorder signal that releases the purchasing agent. Base unit days.",
    "author": "Naga",
    "notes": "s = 50, S = 120, so the order quantity is S - s = 70. Demand is deterministic: 4 customers a day from t=0, 5 units each = 20 units a day. Starting from 80 the stock falls through 50 at t=1.25, the order arrives 1.9 days later with 15 on the shelf and takes it to 85, and that 3.5-day cycle then repeats. Over 34 days: 10 orders placed, 9 received (630 units), 137 customers served (685 units), closing stock 80 + 630 - 685 = 25, and no customer ever waits. Each of the 10 orders carries a 35 EUR ordering cost (a RECORD with kind=cost), so Total Cost is 350 EUR -- a lump sum the engine accrues and itemises in the cost summary, not a rate."
  },
